{"kind":"request","text":"OPS-1: one checked-in command deploys the Workers and checks them\n\nItem 5 of order act fc7576f8. Today the planner deploys four\nWorkers by hand and types the checks. An operator needs one\ncommand and a runbook. No dependency on the identifiers cutover.\nOne head.\n\n1. `scripts/deploy.mjs`. Arguments name the configurations, as in\n   `node scripts/deploy.mjs grow lending demo artroom-scope`. Each\n   name maps to `apps/room/wrangler.\u003cname\u003e.jsonc`. For each one the\n   script:\n   - refuses a checkout with uncommitted changes, and prints HEAD.\n   - runs the pinned Wrangler from a scratch directory outside the\n     checkout. It installs nothing in the checkout.\n   - builds the bundle with a dry run and prints its SHA-256.\n   - compares the `migrations` list of the configuration at HEAD\n     with the list at the commit that the Worker runs. The operator\n     gives that commit, or the previous receipt gives it. The\n     script never guesses it. A new migration tag stops the\n     deployment unless the operator names the tag in\n     `--accept-migration`, because a Durable Object migration is\n     one-way.\n   - deploys with `--keep-vars`.\n   - writes a receipt outside the checkout: commit, configuration,\n     bundle hash, Worker version ID and time.\n   `--dry-run` stops after the bundle hashes. With the hashes of\n   two commits, the operator sees that a landing changed no bundle\n   and needs no deployment.\n\n2. `scripts/deploy-smoke.mjs`. Read-only checks of one deployed\n   Worker, with a browser User-Agent, because the edge answers a\n   scripted client with error 1010:\n   - `/health` three times, each 200. A first 503 after idle is a\n     cold start, and the script retries it once and says so.\n   - `POST /mcp`: 404 while the configuration keeps hosted MCP\n     closed. Read the expectation from the configuration.\n   - `/page/`: 200.\n   - the creation offer names the register of the configuration.\n   The check of `scripts/deploy-check.mjs` stays optional, because\n   it needs an analytics token and dap-lending binds no dataset.\n   The smoke check decides pass or fail.\n\n3. Tests with a scripted Wrangler and a scripted fetch. Named\n   failing cases: a dirty checkout, a new migration tag without\n   `--accept-migration`, a health answer that stays 503, and an\n   open `/mcp` on a closed configuration.\n\n4. A section \"Deploy the hosted Workers\" in\n   docs/operate-a-service.md: the order, the secrets that each\n   Worker needs, the migration rule, the smoke check, rollback and\n   its limit, and the `dap log` and `dap verify` reads of an\n   existing room before and after. Keep it a how-to of commands.\n\nOut of scope: a deployment from CI, any change to a wrangler\nconfiguration, and any deployment by the builder. I run the first\ndeployment with the script after it lands, and I report the result\non this request.\n\nGate once at the head. Checker review at the exact head.","body":{"conditions":"scripts/deploy.mjs deploys named configurations with pinned Wrangler from a scratch directory, guards a new Durable Object migration, and writes a receipt; scripts/deploy-smoke.mjs checks health, closed MCP, the page and the creation offer; tests name four failing cases; docs/operate-a-service.md gains the runbook section. Gate at the head, checker review, no builder deployment.","target_head":"166150ab68fe4fdf1a58920a6fab323015839546","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}